From da85f57c900efd502fec9b67429c084425686105 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:30:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] pf: deliver replies of redirected connections to the host's
 own address

A host connecting to one of its own addresses, with an outbound rule
redirecting the connection to another host, e.g.

	pass out on lo0 proto tcp to <own address> port 30080 rdr-to <container>

(a Kubernetes NodePort reached from the node itself): the SYN leaves
through the container's interface, but the reverse translation of the
replies restores the host's own address as their source, and they arrive
on a non-loopback interface. ip_input()'s source address validation
(net.inet.ip.source_address_validation, on by default) drops them as
spoofed, so the connection never completes.

Such replies match a state created by this host's own outbound packet:
mark inbound IPv4 packets of a translated outbound state whose source and
destination are both local addresses M_FASTFWD_OURS, so ip_input()
delivers them locally. Nothing else is exempted from the check.

Tested on 15.1 arm64: curl from the host to its own address and a port
redirected that way to a container on a bridge: 3/3 succeed (before: the
container's SYN-ACK was dropped and the connect timed out).
---
 sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c b/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c
index 7aee28e7b..a9182b491 100644
--- a/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c
+++ b/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c
@@ -11237,6 +11237,24 @@ pf_test(sa_family_t af, int dir, int pflags, struct ifnet *ifp, struct mbuf **m0
 	    pf_is_loopback(af, pd.dst))
 		pd.m->m_flags |= M_SKIP_FIREWALL;
 
+#ifdef INET
+	/*
+	 * A connection this host made to one of its own addresses that an
+	 * outbound rule redirected to another host (e.g. "pass out on lo0 ...
+	 * rdr-to <container>" for a service published on the host's address):
+	 * the reverse translation of the replies restores the host's own
+	 * address as their source, and they arrive on a non-loopback
+	 * interface, so ip_input()'s source address validation drops them as
+	 * spoofed (net.inet.ip.source_address_validation).  They match a state
+	 * created by this host's own outbound packet, so deliver them locally.
+	 */
+	if (dir == PF_IN && action == PF_PASS && af == AF_INET && s != NULL &&
+	    s->direction == PF_OUT &&
+	    s->key[PF_SK_WIRE] != s->key[PF_SK_STACK] &&
+	    in_localip(pd.src->v4) && in_localip(pd.dst->v4))
+		pd.m->m_flags |= M_FASTFWD_OURS;
+#endif
+
 	if (action == PF_PASS && r->divert.port && !PACKET_LOOPED(&pd)) {
 		mtag = m_tag_alloc(MTAG_PF_DIVERT, 0,
 		    sizeof(struct pf_divert_mtag), M_NOWAIT | M_ZERO);
